**Given:**

The length (in cm) of the transverse common tangent to two circles of radii 2 cm and 5 cm, the centre of the circles being 8 cm apart.

**Formula used:**

Length of transverse common tangent = sqrt{d² - (r₁ + r₂)²}

Where, d = distance between centers, r₁ and r₂ are the radii of the circles.

**Calculations:**

r₁ = 2 cm

r₂ = 5 cm

d = 8 cm

Length of transverse common tangent = sqrt{8² - (2 + 5)²} 

⇒ sqrt{64 - 49}

⇒ sqrt{15}

**∴ The correct answer is option 2.**
